# gridedit, the drawdown (tile) editor of ipl_gprogs, built on the library's vidgets (tieedit): set a cell and a dragged row with the left button,
# clear a cell with the right, shift the tile with a transformation button, turn every symmetry on and set a cell eight ways, write the pattern
# through the File menu and its dialog under a typed name, read the tile's information box from the Drawdown menu, quit with meta q.
# Cell j i of the 10 by 10 grid stands at 123+24j 58+24i.
click 1 207 70
wait
drag 1 135 262 351 262
wait
click 3 135 70
wait
# the first transformation button, shift up
click 1 57 67
wait
# the choice all under symmetries, then one cell
click 1 58 395
wait
click 1 327 94
wait
# the File menu is pulled down and held
move 18 10
press 1
wait
# its item write: a dialog asks the file name
move 30 75
release 1
wait
type t.pat
key Return
wait
# the Drawdown menu, item info: a box with the tile's size and pattern, closed with Return
move 70 10
press 1
wait
move 60 45
release 1
wait
key Return
wait
# meta q ends the editor (the menu's own quit item cannot: its label carries a space the program's case does not)
keydown Alt_L
key q
keyup Alt_L
